# HR360 — TO-BE PROCESS MAPPING

**Document ID:** HR360-BA-004
**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Draft for Review
**Date:** 20 September 2026
**Author:** Nida Khan

# 1. Purpose

This document defines the target-state HR operating model enabled by HR360.

The To-Be model translates approved business requirements and business rules into an integrated HR operating process.

# 2. Target-State Architecture Flow

```text
                         HR360 Users
                              ↓
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │ React Frontend  │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             ↓
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │ REST APIs       │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             ↓
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │ Business Logic  │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             ↓
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │ PostgreSQL      │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             ↓
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │ Analytics APIs  │
                    └────────┬────────┘
                             ↓
                    ┌─────────────────┐
                    │ Dashboards / BI │
                    └─────────────────┘
```

# 3. Employee Management — To-Be

```text
Employee Created
       ↓
Employee Details Captured
       ↓
Department Assigned
       ↓
Job Role Assigned
       ↓
Work Status Assigned
       ↓
Employment Status Maintained
       ↓
PostgreSQL Record
       ↓
API Response
       ↓
Frontend / Reporting
```

# 4. Active Status — To-Be

```text
Employee
   ↓
Identify Department
   ↓
┌─────────────┬──────────────┬──────────────┐
│ HR          │ Operations   │ Finance      │
│             │              │              │
│ EMPLOYED    │ WORKING or   │ SALARY PAID  │
│             │ ONLINE       │              │
└──────┬──────┴───────┬──────┴──────┬───────┘
       ↓              ↓              ↓
            Department Rule
                   ↓
          ACTIVE / NOT ACTIVE
                   ↓
              Analytics
```

# 5. Attendance — To-Be

```text
Employee
   ↓
Attendance Transaction
   ↓
API Validation
   ↓
PostgreSQL
   ↓
Attendance Analytics
   ↓
Dashboard
```

# 6. Leave — To-Be

```text
Employee
   ↓
Create Leave Request
   ↓
Select Leave Type
   ↓
Enter Dates
   ↓
Calculate Duration
   ↓
Approval Workflow
   ↓
Approved / Rejected
   ↓
Leave Analytics
```

# 7. Performance and PIP — To-Be

```text
Employee
   ↓
Performance Review
   ↓
Rating / Feedback
   ↓
Performance Analysis
   ↓
PIP Required?
   ├── No → Continue Monitoring
   │
   └── Yes
        ↓
      Create PIP
        ↓
      Review Period
        ↓
      Progress Monitoring
```

# 8. Training — To-Be

```text
Training Program
       ↓
Employee Enrollment
       ↓
Attendance
       ↓
Completion
       ↓
Score
       ↓
Certificate
       ↓
Training Analytics
```

# 9. Recruitment — To-Be

```text
Candidate
    ↓
Application
    ↓
Screening
    ↓
Shortlisting
    ↓
Interview
    ↓
Interview Result
    ↓
Offer
    ↓
Accepted / Declined
    ↓
Hiring
```

Each stage is represented by structured database records and API operations.

# 10. Analytics — To-Be

```text
Transactional HR Data
        ↓
Analytics APIs
        ↓
KPI Calculations
        ↓
Department / HR Analysis
        ↓
Management Dashboards
        ↓
Power BI
```

# 11. Target-State Benefits

| Area             | Target-State Improvement  |
| ---------------- | ------------------------- |
| Employee data    | Centralized record        |
| Workforce status | Rule-driven calculation   |
| Attendance       | Centralized transaction   |
| Leave            | Structured workflow       |
| Performance      | Centralized history       |
| PIP              | Controlled monitoring     |
| Training         | Centralized participation |
| Recruitment      | End-to-end pipeline       |
| Analytics        | API-driven KPIs           |
| Reporting        | Dashboard-ready data      |

# 12. Target-State Governance

The To-Be process shall follow the principle:

```text
Business Requirement
       ↓
Business Rule
       ↓
Application Workflow
       ↓
Database Transaction
       ↓
Analytics
       ↓
Management Information
```

Changes to business rules should be reflected in the relevant requirements, implementation, test scenarios and analytics definitions.

# 13. Process Improvement Objective

The target-state HR360 model is designed to reduce manual consolidation, improve data consistency and establish traceability between HR transactions and management reporting.

**End of Document**
